---
description: |
  Detects the SOC Prime High-Order Sigma rule "Hospitals, Local Government
  Bodies and FPV Operators - Focus of Cyber Threat Cluster UAC-0247".

  archive -> mshta -> Cscript/Wscript -> Powershell - > scheduled task ->
  system info Enumeration, Initial Access & Staging Chain

  The rule chains 4 stages of SOC Prime behavior rules by host. See
  `socprime::hos::chain` for the correlation and the resulting Detection
  Finding.
args:
  named:
    - name: timeframe
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: The time span that a chain must fit into.
    - name: threshold
      type: float
      default: 0.6
      description: The share of stages a host must cover, between 0 and 1.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 1min
      description: How far findings of a host may arrive out of time order.
---

// Generated by scripts/vendor.py from the SOC Prime HoS rule gTSmKZquRCYV.
let $stages = {
  seq1: [
    "43665ad1-ac11-4069-ad47-7fc26f54acca", // Possible Self-Extracting Archive was Created (via file_event)
    "b3a67b3c-b2f4-49f4-8398-da4734ca9ecb", // Possible Archive Containing Password In The File Name Was Created (via file_event)
  ],
  seq2: [
    "f3bb828c-7019-4b8e-8ef4-212b744ced01", // Suspicious Extracted Files from an Archive (via file_event)
    "ce152116-1d05-408a-a1a7-a4091528dc74", // An Archive Was Extracted To Suspicious Directory Using Powershell (via powershell)
    "9d3c0f31-8fa0-4ebe-ad3f-65cff1e9fb31", // Possible Self-Extracting Archive was Executed (via file_event)
    "2ee3c0b5-8504-4212-b2a8-09e1f95c0bf8", // Windows Shortcut Was Executed With Suspicious Name (via file_event)
  ],
  seq3: [
    "e70092a5-1b91-4a90-9a32-8b94307c9147", // Suspicious LOLBAS MSHTA Defense Evasion Behavior by Detection of Associated Commands (via process_creation)
    "cc7abbd0-762b-41e3-8a26-57ad50d2eea3", // MSHTA Execution with Suspicious File Extensions
    "03cc0c25-389f-4bf8-b48d-11878079f1ca", // Suspicious MSHTA Child Process
    "9387fadc-274f-4326-94f3-cf2eaa539096", // Suspicious Mshta Execution Without HTA File (via cmdline)
    "2907aeac-1558-4538-85a6-6ea9af1548a8", // Suspicious Mshta Execution in an Embedded Mode (via cmdline)
  ],
  seq4: [
    "6917c744-03bc-4abe-92c9-7f87a175c8e6", // Possible Data Infiltration / Exfiltration / C2 via Third Party Services / Tools (via cmdline)
    "342b3e62-2e60-498c-901a-75f56012f02c", // Unusual Top Level Domain In Commandline (via cmdline)
    "93ec52aa-776a-4976-8209-bc68321c75b7", // Possible Data Exfiltration over WebRequests (via powershell)
    "69b6437e-cee7-4b31-a02b-537356cff33d", // Download or Upload via Powershell (via cmdline)
